                                 Introduction
                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
Have you ever wanted to give your users a choice between viewing a lot of
bulls(hit) at login or just loggin in fast? If yes, then this is the door
you've been looking for.


                                 Installation
                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
Just copy the contents of the archive to your BBS: directory or install the
door manually as an XIM.

Then you need to modify your BBS:Bull.txt to look something like this:

--CUT--
~
~CC_QLOGON
--CUT--

Now you just need to configure the QuickLogon with these tooltypes:
"QUICK" this is the path of the loginscript used when choosing a quicklogon.

"NOQUICK" this is the path when choosing a normal logon.

"SHOW_ALL" this is the path of the loginscript that will be showed to
everyone. Use this for stuff that should otherwise have been in both the
QUICK-text and the NOQUICK-text. Leave out this tooltype if you don't want to
use it.

"FORCE.{baud}" this is the path of the loginscripts that will be forced upon a
certain baudrate, so you can eg. have large ansi-logins for your 14400+ users
and a normal ascii-login for your 2400 users. Leave out this tooltype if you
don't want to use it.


And that's about it for the installation. Look at the supplied files if you
need more info.


